WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.660
I used the back side.

3
00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.560
They're fine.

4
00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.360
[NAMI]
I hope you're
proud of yourself,

5
00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.360
beating those
poor shipwrights!

6
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.330
[CHOPPER]
You're so strong, Zoro!

7
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.470
Whatever. Might
as well go ahead!

8
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.800
[CHOPPER]
Zoro! This way!

9
00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.840
[ZORO]
Got it.

10
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.370
No! Over here!

11
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.370
We're leading the
way for you, stupid!

12
00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.310
How can you get lost already?!

13
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:29.800
<b>The Six Powers</b>

14
00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.920
Easy! 'Cause I'm rubber!

15
00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.460
All right.
Good. Now help me.

16
00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:42.960
[LUFFY]
No prob!

17
00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:50.370
You're gonna pay
you masked bastards.

18
00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.440
[LUCCI]
It's true,

19
00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.310
we've been undercover
for the last five years.

20
00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.960
Ah, but don't worry,

21
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.960
we took our jobs as
shipwrights very seriously.

22
00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.550
I understand how shocked you must be.

23
00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.870
However, we can't
devote any more

24
00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.340
time to this matter.

25
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.900
We will achieve our goal by any means
necessary.

26
00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:17.410
So if you're thinking
about resisting

27
00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.450
for the sake of
being difficult,

28
00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.410
I suggest you reconsider
for your own good

29
00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.310
as well as ours.

30
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.980
I assume you're already
familiar with Cipher Pol.

31
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.170
It's the government's
supreme intelligence agency

32
00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.530
with eight branches.

33
00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.000
Their worldwide bases

34
00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.240
are referred to as
CP1 through CP8.

35
00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.170
Together, they serve
as the government's eyes

36
00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:42.080
and ears in every
corner of the globe.

37
00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.630
Of course I know.

38
00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.400
But how do all of you fit into that
picture?

39
00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.580
[LUCCI]
Good question.

40
00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.590
As the 9th Cipher Pol unit,
we officially do not exist.

41
00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.860
And by virtue of that,

42
00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:56.520
we possess a certain privilege
that the other branches lack.

43
00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.960
One that necessitates a degree of secrecy.

44
00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.000
A "privilege"?

45
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.100
[LUCCI]
That's right.

46
00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.470
Consider it a blade we wield in the name
of justice.

47
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:10.200
If a citizen is "uncooperative"
towards the government,

48
00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.560
we may execute them.

49
00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:14.980
You fools.

50
00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.920
You can't use justice as an excuse for
murder!

51
00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.060
[LUCCI]
Recently, the
government has been forced

52
00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.240
to change its way of thinking.

53
00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.450
For example, rather than
fearing Pluton's revival

54
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.440
they have decided
to awaken it,

55
00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:30.010
to use the ancient weapon
as a force of justice

56
00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.250
that can bring an end
to the Great Pirate Era.

57
00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.080
And now, for some reason,

58
00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.760
you want to stand in their way.

59
00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.130
It's almost as if
you have no sympathy

60
00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.250
for all of the people constantly
being victimized by pirates.

61
00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:45.360
You should reconsider where your loyalties
lie.

62
00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.660
Don't kid yourself.

63
00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:48.120
If the weapon is restored,

64
00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.520
the world is going to
fight over its power.

65
00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.860
It will only breed more destruction.

66
00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:57.700
Are you saying you don't trust
the government, Mr. Iceburg?

67
00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.540
That would be a shame.

68
00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.640
Not at all. It's human nature
that I don't trust, Lucci.

69
00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.150
Show some respect!

70
00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:17.420
Remember, you're not my boss anymore.

71
00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.840
Kaku, check his pulse.

72
00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.020
'Scuse me.

73
00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.420
[LUCCI]
Here's the situation.

74
00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:33.780
A while ago we
came up with a bit

75
00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.920
of a hypothesis
about the blueprints.

76
00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.070
All you have to do is lie there

77
00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.570
and listen to our hypothesis
without saying a word.

78
00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.140
Even if your mouth
won't cooperate,

79
00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.710
your pulse will
tell us the truth.

80
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.270
[LUCCI]
Now that
we're all comfortable,

81
00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.900
let me explain
the thought process

82
00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.210
leading to our hypothesis.

83
00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.910
First of all, the way
that you allowed us

84
00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.710
to retrieve the fake blueprints
is highly suspicious.

85
00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.080
After you decided
that the culprits

86
00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.680
were related to the government,

87
00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:06.420
you intentionally revealed
the location of the fakes,

88
00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:09.150
presumably in the
hopes of fooling us.

89
00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:11.730
However, what if your
assumption was wrong

90
00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.500
and the culprit's
intention was to kill you

91
00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.070
rather than to
retrieve the blueprints?

92
00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.100
In that case, the
fakes would be useless,

93
00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.840
the real blueprints
would be lost

94
00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.770
and the will of the
original shipwrights

95
00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.780
would not be passed on.

96
00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:26.210
Surely you considered that possibility.

97
00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.250
I know you're no fool.

98
00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.210
And yet, despite
creating a decoy,

99
00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.030
you've seemingly
made no attempt

100
00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.300
to pass off the actual
blueprints tonight.

101
00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.210
That must mean you've already entrusted
them to someone.

102
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.080
[steady heartbeat]

103
00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:41.880
We still don't know
where they are,

104
00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.450
but we can assume
that you don't have them

105
00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:44.800
with you anymore.

106
00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.140
That's our hypothesis.

107
00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.940
Ah-ah! No squirming.

108
00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:53.910
[LUCCI]
This is still just a theory.

109
00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.850
I admit.

110
00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.720
We haven't found any
decisive evidence.

111
00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.460
And despite the
fact that we've kept

112
00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:02.450
you under surveillance
for the past five years.

113
00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.960
We've never seen you
do anything suspicious.

114
00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.560
Assuming you did entrust
the blueprints to someone,

115
00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.700
they would have to be an
accomplished shipwright

116
00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.010
to make any
sense out of them.

117
00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:14.310
[steady heartbeat]

118
00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:20.220
Now if we add that to our theory
things start to get interesting.

119
00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.230
For example,
let's take a closer look

120
00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:25.330
at the fake blueprints
that you left us.

121
00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:26.560
Here at the bottom,

122
00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:30.250
you can see the signatures of
three different shipwrights.

123
00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.320
"Tom," "Iceburg,"
and "Cutty Flam."

124
00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.970
And the company
name "Tom's Workers."

125
00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.390
You probably thought that this
detail wouldn't mean anything

126
00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.060
to whoever took the bait

127
00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:44.280
but you had no idea your
enemies were so close.

128
00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:47.380
That was a grave miscalculation on your
part.

129
00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:50.050
If the person who broke
in had been an outsider,

130
00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.850
once they found out
that the blueprints

131
00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.830
had nothing to do with Pluton,

132
00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.140
they would probably
have throw them away.

133
00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:57.000
However.

134
00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.910
Since we've been
shipwrights ourselves

135
00:07:58.940 --> 00:07:59.980
for the past five years,

136
00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.120
the names of the designers are very
interesting.

137
00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.100
There's a visitor,
sir to see you.

138
00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.130
[steady heartbeat]

139
00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.200
[LUCCI]
Although
many people know

140
00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:12.400
of the legendary
shipwright, Tom,

141
00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:16.420
the details of his actual
company are shrouded in mystery.

142
00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.010
It's believed to have
existed on this island,

143
00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:22.280
but there's no roster
or register to be found.

144
00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.180
It was no easy task finding out

145
00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.100
that you were one
of Tom's apprentices.

146
00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:30.430
What few reports
we have indicate

147
00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.200
that he taught only
two shipwrights.

148
00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.000
And a government
official verified

149
00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:39.330
that one of them died in
an accident 8 years ago.

150
00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.030
[KOKORO]
Real shame.

151
00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.600
I know Cutty Flam was
a bit of a loose cannon,

152
00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:48.500
but I sure hate to see him go.

153
00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.970
[LUCCI]
It struck a chord.
I thought to myself

154
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.210
"now where have
I heard that name before?"

155
00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.310
[steady heartbeat]

156
00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:58.140
He said he's a friend from years back.

157
00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.570
Do you know anyone
named "Cutty Flam"?

158
00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.640
[ICEBURG]
It was about four years ago,

159
00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:07.390
shortly after we started
our undercover operation.

160
00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.120
He was a man who
has passed through

161
00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:12.250
Galley-La's gates
many times since.

162
00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:15.590
But only once did he ever use that name.

163
00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:17.160
I remember it clearly.

164
00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:18.530
So do I.

165
00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.270
[steady heartbeat]

166
00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:21.870
[KALIFA]
Shall I show him in, sir?

167
00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:24.540
No, turn him away.

168
00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.170
[LUCCI]
In other words.

169
00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:40.100
Tom's second apprentice,
Cutty Flam, is still alive...

170
00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:42.350
And living in
this town no less.

171
00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.870
But now, he goes by "Franky."

172
00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:54.980
[rapid heartbeat]

173
00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:56.410
[FRANKY]
What's with all the secrecy?

174
00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:58.050
Something going on?

175
00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.520
Huh?

176
00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:04.490
Hey what're these?

177
00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:07.330
The blueprints for that old battleship?

178
00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.930
[ICEBURG]
Don't call
yourself Cutty Flam anymore.

179
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.300
Huh?

180
00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:12.400
It's only a matter of time

181
00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:15.100
before the
government targets me.

182
00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:19.200
I want you to take these and leave this
island, Franky.

183
00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:22.340
Seems pretty obvious now, huh?

184
00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.370
[KAKU]
I can't believe
it took us all these years

185
00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.130
to figure out the connection.

186
00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:30.170
Our searches on him turned up nothing.

187
00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.000
I must admit that
his true identity

188
00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.210
was a well-hidden secret.

189
00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.310
And because he's an oaf
and a ship dismantler,

190
00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.980
we never really
gave him much thought.

191
00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:42.320
It's ironic, really. Since we
never questioned our reports,

192
00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.080
it didn't occur to
us that a dead person

193
00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.220
might actually still be alive.

194
00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:49.290
The setup was quite
convenient for you, I imagine.

195
00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.520
Since the Franky family
often came to the shipyard

196
00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.730
to sell lumber, there
were plenty of chances

197
00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.860
to pass off the blueprints.

198
00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:58.830
You managed it well, he was
close when you needed him,

199
00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.730
yet always at a safe distance.

200
00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:02.730
That would also explain why

201
00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.260
you were so confident
in dealing with us.

202
00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.020
You knew that we were
looking for the blueprints

203
00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:08.960
in the wrong place.

204
00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.210
And while it might seem strange

205
00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.780
that your most trusted foremen
had not heard of the blueprints,

206
00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:15.600
they couldn't possibly
be as close to you

207
00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:17.960
as Tom's other apprentice.

208
00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.770
From this line of thinking, everything
checks out.

209
00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.270
Not only that.

210
00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:26.570
Your racing pulse has confirmed
that our hypothesis is true!

211
00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:30.720
C'mon, hurry!

212
00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.030
[ZORO]
Hey!

213
00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:33.420
You sure this's the right way?

214
00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.250
Don't even go there!

215
00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:40.750
Their injuries are pretty bad.

216
00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.380
All right, that's gotta be it...

217
00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.210
the closed door at
the end of the hallway!

218
00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.100
Looks like a lotta people
got hurt guarding that door!

219
00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:53.240
[ZORO]
Hmm? Uh... Hey...

220
00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.170
What're you waiting for?

221
00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.010
Cut down the door and beat the bad guys!

222
00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.110
We're right behind you!

223
00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.210
Hurry it up!

224
00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:01.160
All right, I'll do it,
but not cause you told me to!

225
00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.760
Hey, Straw Hat! Wait!

226
00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:05.220
[loud crash]

227
00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.960
YAAAAAA!

228
00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:08.730
This is the wrong room, you idiot!

229
00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.660
It's the one next door!
You hear me? Ugh...

230
00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.760
Yeah? Oh. Oops.

231
00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.370
[LUCCI]
Don't blame yourself.

232
00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.240
You're only human.

233
00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.970
And under these circumstances,

234
00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.180
no one would be able to hide
the truth from us for very long.

235
00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.280
So just be grateful that justice will
prevail in the end.

236
00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.380
Thanks so much for
the last five years.

237
00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.400
But you've outlived
your usefulness.

238
00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:33.260
Let's find Franky before the storm hits.

239
00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:35.940
You bastards!

240
00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:38.940
Hm?

241
00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:49.240
Give Robin back!

242
00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.240
Luffy!

243
00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.780
Luffy?

244
00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.110
You again?

245
00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:03.030
Robin! I finally found you!

246
00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.300
Hey, Luffy!

247
00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.530
Where were you when we had to
beat up all those shipwrights?!

248
00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:10.170
Robin! Why did you leave us?!

249
00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:13.900
Hold on a sec.
Something's not right here.

250
00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.190
Well, well, well...

251
00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:25.140
Paulie, Straw Hat.

252
00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.670
[PAULIE]
Iceburg.

253
00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:32.000
What is this?

254
00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:38.910
[PAULIE]
What the hell's going on?!

255
00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:50.610
Paulie, damn it.
You should've run.

256
00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.410
No. What?

257
00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.010
This doesn't make sense.

258
00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:58.150
You're makin' it
look like, like...

259
00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:01.550
You guys were the ones
who were after Iceburg.

260
00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:04.120
But that can't be right!

261
00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.050
Auuugh!

262
00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:12.790
What hell are you doing
with those weird costumes on?

263
00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:15.660
Stop screwing with me here!

264
00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:17.290
Hey! Kalifa!

265
00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:22.260
Blueno! Kaku! Lucci!
Say something already, damn it!

266
00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.200
Oh yeah!
Those are the same guys

267
00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:30.370
that were with you back at
the shipyard, right? Right?

268
00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:33.840
Actually. That square-nose
guy came to our ship.

269
00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:37.740
I see. Then the attack on
Iceburg was an inside job.

270
00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.940
Wait, what? I don't get it.

271
00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.610
Paulie in all honesty,

272
00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:46.340
we're secret agents working
for the World Government.

273
00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:49.610
But hey, you'll forgive me if I say I'm
sorry, right?

274
00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:51.780
We were comrades,

275
00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:55.760
building ships together
every day from dawn til' dusk.

276
00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.130
I realize this is
quite sudden for you,

277
00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:03.100
so perhaps you'd believe me
if I smashed Iceburg's face?

278
00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.240
[PAULIE]
Just shut the hell up.

279
00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.110
I've heard enough.

280
00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:12.790
You were that guy in the bull mask,
weren't you?

281
00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:15.830
That was the first time I ever heard your
voice.

282
00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:19.160
All those years, you never said a word.

283
00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:21.290
But you can talk just fine!

284
00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.000
I'll teach you to make fun of me!

285
00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:25.830
Paulie, stop it!

286
00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:30.400
Pipe Hitch Knives!

287
00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.240
Finger Pistol!

288
00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:50.130
[LUCCI]
You still haven't
learned your lesson, have you?

289
00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:59.850
Hey! Are you okay?!

290
00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:03.220
Screw you...

291
00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:04.820
Lucci.

292
00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:15.190
[LUCCI]
It's pointless to resist.

293
00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:18.020
Our abilities far exceed
those of a normal human,

294
00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.920
as you can see.

295
00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.230
After many years of training,

296
00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:24.030
we've mastered an art
called the "Six Powers."

297
00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:26.100
These techniques
transform the body

298
00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:29.770
into a living weapon with
the strength of over 100 men.

299
00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:37.310
Coo coo! Stop drinking, Paulie!
What about all that debt!

300
00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:42.000
C'mon, I won some cash today.
Next round's on me, okay?

301
00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:44.900
Bring it, Blueno! Let's go!

302
00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:46.770
You got it!

303
00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:57.610
Kalifa, you hussy!
That skirt is way too short!

304
00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.220
[chuckles]

305
00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:00.990
Hey, give it a rest, Paulie!

306
00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.820
If you don't like it,
don't look at her.

307
00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:03.630
'Kay?

308
00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:06.160
[chuckles]

309
00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:16.570
[PAULIE]
After all this time, why?

310
00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:19.480
Sorry, Paulie.

311
00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.120
Our friendship is over.

312
00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:25.220
I have to eliminate you.

313
00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.360
Lucci! No! Don't!

314
00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:32.330
You jerk! Leave him alone!

315
00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:41.740
Iron Body.

316
00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.840
...Gatling!

317
00:17:50.890 --> 00:17:53.800
What the... That
didn't work at all!

318
00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:03.440
You're nothing
but a pest. Shave!

319
00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.240
He's gone.

320
00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:12.010
Finger Pistol!

321
00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.700
[LUFFY coughs]

322
00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.340
If you weren't
made out of rubber,

323
00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:39.910
you'd be dead with
a hole in your neck.

324
00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:41.610
Lucky you.

325
00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.420
You're protecting him. But why?

326
00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:01.660
Why not?! Because
I don't want you to kill him!

327
00:19:01.690 --> 00:19:04.000
You guys were all
friends just the other day,

328
00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.700
how could you do this?!

329
00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:13.140
We were. Now,
things have changed.

330
00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.740
It doesn't matter,
you can say what you want.

331
00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:18.180
You're a bunch of traitors.

332
00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.950
The point is,
you're my enemy now.

333
00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:23.120
I made a promise with
Paulie to beat the crap

334
00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:26.970
out of anybody who
tries to hurt Ice Pops!

335
00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:31.370
I see. You decided to
trust him over us, huh?

336
00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.310
That's right.

337
00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:35.740
'Cause you guys took
away one of my friends!

338
00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:39.820
Hey, Robin, what gives?
Why're you acting like this?

339
00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:43.050
If you wanna leave the crew,
at least tell me why!

340
00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:44.720
Yeah! And why would
you want to team up

341
00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:47.350
with people from the world
government?! That's crazy!

342
00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:49.420
Do I have to repeat myself?

343
00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.720
I believe I said my farewells

344
00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.390
to the Cook and the
Doctor before I left.

345
00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.230
Didn't you pass that along, Chopper?

346
00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:56.330
'Course I did!

347
00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.120
But just because I heard it doesn't mean I
accept it!

348
00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.090
How could you do this?

349
00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:03.430
I did it to make my wish come true.

350
00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:06.160
A wish that can't happen as long as we're
together.

351
00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:09.370
And if you can't
accept that I'm sorry.

352
00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:13.160
[ROBIN]
You may not find it
fair but to accomplish my goal.

353
00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:16.360
I'll make any sacrifice!

354
00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.700
I see. And that includes framing

355
00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.000
your own crewmates
for attempted murder.

356
00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:22.700
So what is this wish of yours?

357
00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.310
I don't have to answer that question.

358
00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:27.850
[ICEBURG]
Are you out of your mind?

359
00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.790
Wake up, Robin.

360
00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.620
You have no right to do this!

361
00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.530
I don't care what it is
you're trying to accomplish.

362
00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:36.500
The consequences
are far too great!

363
00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.400
I've heard enough!

364
00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:41.630
This is no longer your choice to make!

365
00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:45.170
This should shut you up.

366
00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:46.800
No! Iceburg!

367
00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.810
I won't let anyone
get in my way!

368
00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.360
Nothing you're saying is making any sense!

369
00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:16.430
You expect me to believe this?!

370
00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.600
Robin! What happened to you?!

371
00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:29.280
You're our friend, right?
Please, Robin! Come back!

372
00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:33.510
Sorry to break
up the reunion,

373
00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:36.150
but I'll have
to stop you there.

374
00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:38.750
You see, we have a
date this evening

375
00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:40.550
with a very
important individual.

376
00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:43.160
One that's been over
four years in the making.

377
00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:44.660
We're finished here.

378
00:21:44.690 --> 00:21:49.360
In other words, that means we're
finished with you, as well.

379
00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:56.490
Kalifa, how much time is left?

380
00:21:56.490 --> 00:21:57.670
Two minutes.

381
00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.660
Here's the deal.
I know this is sudden,

382
00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:01.660
but in two minutes,

383
00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:03.830
this building will go
up in a ball of flame.

384
00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:05.430
Huh?

385
00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:06.930
[gasps]

386
00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.060
You're kidding.

387
00:22:08.100 --> 00:22:09.330
[LUCCI]
Of course not.

388
00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:13.400
Fire is an effective tool for erasing all
sorts of evidence.

389
00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:14.800
If you don't want
to be burned alive,

390
00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:18.670
I suggest you leave the
building as soon as possible.

391
00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:20.980
Well, I say that...

392
00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:27.040
...but I have no intention
of letting you go.

393
00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:34.050
Looks like it's gonna
be us against them,

394
00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:37.890
and our "friend" Robin has
clearly picked her side.

395
00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:41.590
Luffy, Robin is not
one of us anymore,

396
00:22:41.640 --> 00:22:43.840
do you accept that now?

397
00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.040
No! No way!

398
00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:52.850
So noisy.

399
00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:55.420
Anyway, the first floor is about to set
fire.

400
00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:57.020
It won't be pretty.

401
00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.380
But to be fair, the
culprits are just pirates,

402
00:23:00.410 --> 00:23:02.610
you can't expect
them to be subtle.

403
00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:04.550
You bastards!

404
00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:10.750
That's nice of you to give us
credit for your attempted arson.

405
00:23:10.790 --> 00:23:12.520
But I think that I'll pass!

406
00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:13.460
What's one more crime,

407
00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:16.990
when we're going to
execute you anyway?

408
00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:23.570
[ROBIN]
Well...

409
00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:25.770
I suppose I'll take
my leave now.

410
00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:29.610
You've done exactly as
you were told. Good work.

411
00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:33.450
Robin! Don't go!
You're still one of us!

412
00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:35.420
This is farewell.

413
00:23:35.460 --> 00:23:36.960
Robin!

414
00:23:39.700 --> 00:23:42.140
Stop her...

415
00:23:42.170 --> 00:23:43.840
Straw Hat.

416
00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.110
[LUFFY]
We finally found you.
I won't let you run away again!

417
00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:51.060
Outta my way!

418
00:23:51.060 --> 00:23:51.700
Iron Body.

419
00:23:57.720 --> 00:24:01.390
How come nothing I do to
these guys even phases them?!

420
00:24:03.270 --> 00:24:05.080
In addition to our
offensive techniques,

421
00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:07.310
our training has also
given us the ability

422
00:24:07.350 --> 00:24:11.120
to make our body as solid as an iron wall.

423
00:24:11.150 --> 00:24:11.950
Of course.

424
00:24:11.980 --> 00:24:14.350
Your punches are
weak to begin with.

425
00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:16.990
Okay, whatever, I said.

426
00:24:17.020 --> 00:24:18.360
Outta my way!

427
00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.020
Paper Art.

428
00:24:29.590 --> 00:24:32.460
Whoa! Even though
he's big he sure is fast!

429
00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:35.660
He's moving like his body's made of paper!

430
00:24:39.100 --> 00:24:40.770
Oh no.

431
00:24:40.800 --> 00:24:42.000
Robin!

432
00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:47.970
Move it!

433
00:24:48.010 --> 00:24:50.080
Gum-Gum...

434
00:24:50.100 --> 00:24:52.670
...Pistol!

435
00:24:52.700 --> 00:24:53.900
[BLUENO]
Shave!

436
00:24:55.440 --> 00:24:56.840
He disappeared!

437
00:24:59.540 --> 00:25:00.510
My legs are so strong

438
00:25:00.540 --> 00:25:03.880
that I can move faster
than your eyes can see.

439
00:25:04.450 --> 00:25:05.650
[LUFFY]
Stand still!

440
00:25:05.690 --> 00:25:07.130
Moon Walk.

441
00:25:07.240 --> 00:25:11.540
In fact, I can even leap off of the air
itself.

442
00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:14.860
He's flying!

443
00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:18.450
Tempest...

444
00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:19.980
...Kick!

445
00:25:23.800 --> 00:25:24.830
[ZORO]
A slashing attack?

446
00:25:24.990 --> 00:25:27.030
Get down! Hurry!

447
00:25:27.060 --> 00:25:28.960
Why?

448
00:25:42.230 --> 00:25:44.140
Luffy!

449
00:25:44.710 --> 00:25:47.510
They did all that with
a single kick? No way!

450
00:25:47.550 --> 00:25:48.450
[KALIFA]
Technically, it was

451
00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:50.980
the sharp gust of
wind that followed it.

452
00:25:51.020 --> 00:25:53.950
We call it the "Tempest Kick."

453
00:26:00.330 --> 00:26:02.720
We met on your ship,
didn't we, Roronoa?

454
00:26:05.710 --> 00:26:08.630
You said, you people
aren't real shipwrights?

455
00:26:09.610 --> 00:26:12.880
So does that mean you
lied about the Merry, too?

456
00:26:13.320 --> 00:26:17.820
Unfortunately not, I was quite
honest about my assessment.

457
00:26:18.370 --> 00:26:20.470
I'm sorry to hear that.

458
00:26:36.990 --> 00:26:39.070
[LUFFY]
Don't go, Robin!

459
00:26:39.450 --> 00:26:42.620
We're not done talking yet!

460
00:26:42.650 --> 00:26:47.620
No. It's over. This is
the last time you'll see me.

461
00:26:47.660 --> 00:26:49.660
Robin!

462
00:26:58.480 --> 00:26:59.750
Luffy! Go after Robin.

463
00:26:59.780 --> 00:27:02.190
Whatever happens, don't let her get away!

464
00:27:10.930 --> 00:27:12.400
Confident, huh?

465
00:27:12.460 --> 00:27:15.360
You really shouldn't
take your eyes off of me!

466
00:27:18.820 --> 00:27:20.320
Zoro!

467
00:27:23.580 --> 00:27:25.340
[KAKU]
Finger Pistol.

468
00:27:29.280 --> 00:27:32.850
It turns out there are some things more
deadly than bullets.

469
00:27:37.560 --> 00:27:39.350
[LUFFY]
What's your problem?!

470
00:27:39.350 --> 00:27:42.250
Get out of my way!

471
00:27:42.290 --> 00:27:44.920
All those punches, and
he's not even blinking!

472
00:27:44.960 --> 00:27:47.520
[LUCCI]
I have him. Now go.

473
00:27:56.470 --> 00:27:58.170
Robin!

474
00:28:17.210 --> 00:28:18.540
[NAMI]
Luffy!

475
00:28:18.670 --> 00:28:19.800
[CHOPPER]
Zoro!

476
00:28:28.180 --> 00:28:32.140
I don't believe it.
How can they be so strong?

477
00:28:32.250 --> 00:28:36.090
I knew you were tough,
but this's too much.

478
00:28:36.120 --> 00:28:38.190
We're not like you.

479
00:28:38.590 --> 00:28:42.240
As members of CP9, for as
long as we can remember,

480
00:28:42.700 --> 00:28:46.530
we've trained to surpass
the limits of the human body.

481
00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:48.130
And vowed to hone those skills

482
00:28:48.170 --> 00:28:51.140
into an instrument
of absolute justice.

483
00:28:51.360 --> 00:28:52.820
[LUCCI]
The results of that training

484
00:28:52.860 --> 00:28:57.830
are the superhuman techniques
known as the Six Powers.

485
00:28:57.860 --> 00:29:00.500
So now, I'm sure it's
abundantly clear to you,

486
00:29:00.530 --> 00:29:04.640
why the four of us are the
government's most elite agents.

487
00:29:04.670 --> 00:29:05.840
And by the same token,

488
00:29:05.870 --> 00:29:08.470
you must also realize
how miserably weak

489
00:29:08.510 --> 00:29:11.680
a band of pirates
is in comparison.

490
00:29:19.480 --> 00:29:21.590
[LUCCI]
Of course, the
full extent of our powers

491
00:29:21.650 --> 00:29:24.620
is strictly classified
but rest assured,

492
00:29:24.650 --> 00:29:27.690
scum like you would
never make the cut.

493
00:29:30.510 --> 00:29:31.450
[KALIFA]
Lucci.

494
00:29:31.730 --> 00:29:34.360
The ignition device
is about to detonate.

495
00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:35.670
We should probably hurry.

496
00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:37.170
Hmph.

497
00:29:37.200 --> 00:29:40.340
But a chance like this one is quite rare.

498
00:29:40.350 --> 00:29:42.420
Let me show you something interesting.

499
00:29:45.520 --> 00:29:47.130
devil fruit powers!

500
00:29:49.020 --> 00:29:49.930
Which one is it?

501
00:29:57.790 --> 00:30:01.600
Lucci. What in the...?

502
00:30:03.320 --> 00:30:05.380
[LUCCI]
Cat-Cat Fruit.

503
00:30:09.070 --> 00:30:11.610
The Leopard model.

504
00:30:13.580 --> 00:30:15.440
A human leopard!

505
00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:16.980
He's huge!

506
00:30:19.540 --> 00:30:25.580
What's going on here?
What in the hell are you?!
